# Styling: Design tokens + Tailwind + Ant Design theming

## Color system
All colors come from **design tokens** defined in `src/styles/design-tokens.css`.
They are mapped to Tailwind utilities in `src/index.css` via `@theme inline`.

```
Token variable (CSS)    → Tailwind class
var(--background)       → bg-background
var(--foreground)       → text-foreground
var(--primary)          → bg-primary, text-primary
var(--border)           → border-border
var(--muted-fg)         → text-muted-foreground
var(--ff-success)       → text-success
var(--ff-error)         → text-error
```

## Rules

### No hardcoded hex/rgb values in components
```tsx
// WRONG
<div style={{ color: '#2563EB' }}>
<span className="text-[#475569]">

// RIGHT
<div className="text-primary">
<span className="text-muted-foreground">
```

Exception: `src/lib/antd-theme.ts` and `src/styles/design-tokens.css` are the ONLY files where raw hex values belong. Ant Design cannot read CSS variables at runtime, so its theme config must use hex duplicates.

### Use Tailwind utility classes
- Layout: `flex`, `grid`, `gap-*`, `p-*`, `m-*`, `space-y-*`
- Text: `text-sm`, `text-xs`, `font-medium`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`
- Borders: `border`, `border-border`, `rounded`, `rounded-lg`
- Sizing: `w-full`, `h-full`, `min-h-0`, `flex-1`

### No inline styles unless dynamic
```tsx
// WRONG — static styling via inline
<div style={{ padding: '16px', borderRadius: '6px' }}>

// RIGHT — Tailwind
<div className="p-4 rounded-md">

// OK — genuinely dynamic
<div style={{ width: `${percentage}%` }}>
```

### Dark mode
- Handled by `.dark` class on `<html>` element (toggled by `useThemeStore`).
- Tailwind: use `dark:` variant when needed, but prefer semantic token colors that auto-switch.
- Ant Design: `ConfigProvider` receives `darkTheme` or `lightTheme` from `src/lib/antd-theme.ts`.
- CSS overrides for Ant portaled components (e.g. `.ant-message`): put in `src/index.css` with `html.dark` selector.

### Spacing and layout tokens
```css
--space-1: 4px   --space-2: 8px   --space-3: 12px
--space-4: 16px  --space-6: 24px  --space-8: 32px
--nav-height: 48px  --radius: 6px  --page-padding: 24px
```
Use Tailwind equivalents: `p-1` (4px), `p-2` (8px), `gap-4` (16px), `gap-6` (24px).

### Typography
- Primary font: `'Inter'` (via `--font-sans`).
- Grid font: `'Roboto'` (via `--font-grid`) — used in data tables.
- Never add new Google Font imports without discussion.

### Global behavior for shared primitives (consistency)
Patterns that should feel the same everywhere (scroll, max height, spacing for overlays, focus rings, etc.) **must be solved once globally**, not per screen.

- **Ant Design `Modal`, `Drawer`, and similar portaled components:** Prefer shared overrides in `src/styles/design-tokens.css` (or `src/index.css` when tied to `#root` / `html.dark`) and/or `ConfigProvider` `theme.components` in `src/lib/antd-theme.ts`.
- **Do not** add one-off `styles={{ body: … }}`, `classNames`, or ad-hoc `max-height` / `overflow` on a single modal to fix layout — that causes inconsistent UX (e.g. one modal scrolls, another stretches past the viewport).
- **If** a single instance truly needs different behavior, document why in a short code comment and prefer a **reusable** pattern (e.g. a wrapper in `src/components/ui-kit/`, or a dedicated `rootClassName` convention) rather than copying inline fixes across files.
- **Current example:** modal max-height + scrollable body live under the “All modals (Ant Design 6+)” block in `design-tokens.css` (`.ant-modal-container`, `.ant-modal-body`, etc.). Extend that block when adjusting modal behavior for the whole app.
- **Form dialogs:** put actions in **`Modal`’s `footer`** so they stay fixed while the body scrolls; see `open-ui-uikit-components.mdc` (form + `formId` / submit button pattern).

### Icons
- Use **`lucide-react`** for icons (consistent across the app).
- Import individual icons: `import { Plus, Trash2 } from 'lucide-react'`
- Standard size in buttons: `className="h-3.5 w-3.5"` or `className="h-4 w-4"`

## Never
- Never use arbitrary Tailwind values for colors (`text-[#xxx]`) — add a token if the color is new.
- Never import from `@ant-design/icons` — use `lucide-react`.
- Never set `style={{ color: '...' }}` for colors that exist as tokens.
- Never create new CSS files — extend `design-tokens.css` for new variables or `index.css` for global overrides.
- Never fix overlay/modal layout (scroll, viewport cap, mask) in isolation on one feature component when the same primitive is used app-wide — update the global rules above instead.
